b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 59\u00b0F, and the record is 79\u00b0F (1931). The low of <strong>40\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Charlottesville's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Charlottesville has set <strong>85 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 78 that chance alone would give, and <strong>76 record highs</strong>, close to the 79 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (57). Charlottesville's all-time high is 107\u00b0F, on July 20, 1930.","t_chg":"Charlottesville's days and nights have warmed since 1986","p_chg":"Across 95 complete years: Charlottesville's average low shows no clear change: +0.01\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.08 to +0.10) that includes zero. Charlottesville's average high shows no clear change: +0.09\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.01 to +0.19) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.87\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.46 to +1.28) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.63\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.16 to +1.10). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months. Highs rose in 4 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Charlottesville's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.69 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 41.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 1937 (72.07 in); the driest, 1988 (14.90 in). Charlottesville almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is nan inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 8 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}